  [ledge] 17.87 mm² flat face 0° off facing the bed · 5.8 × 5.8 mm · 4.2 mm up
    file: hardware/printed-parts/cold-core/reservoir/reservoir-cap-left.step
    face: plane · n x=0.000 y=0.000 z=1.000 · thru x=-124.316 y=-66.020 z=4.750
    click: x=-124.316 y=-66.020 z=4.750
    answered: The six flat counterbore floors are the M3 socket-head bearing faces. Their 5.8 mm diameter and depth seat the selected screw heads below the exterior face; these retained hardware seats require flat head contact.
    alternatives: Sloping the floors removes the screw-head bearing plane. Filling the counterbores makes the heads project into the 0.4 mm gap beneath the foam cap.

